WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.319
In this video we are going to talk about
an important device in networking called

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:10.139
a 'network interface card' or NIC. So
before we talk about that I want to give

00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:15.120
you an example of how humans communicate. Now imagine we have three different people:

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.070
John, Bob, and Mary. How did they talk? When you're talking you're using your mouth.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:25.230
So you're transmitting information using
the mouth and the other person is

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:31.470
receiving the information through their
ears. Now, how do computers, y'know, talk or

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:37.739
listen? They have a device called 'network
interface card' which acts as the ear

00:00:37.739 --> 00:00:44.550
and the mouth of the computer. So that's
how computers talk through the 'network

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.360
interface card.'

